<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic52205e37cae13d1cc7aaae4b35a634382fb6f66" commit="cc09d2d8b16995a10b8f349b7424c2ee43711824" commit_message="Add D-Bus constants for VirtualFileProvider  Add D-Bus constants for VirtualFileProvider service and VirtualFileRequestHandlerService (which is implemented as part of chrome).  BUG=chromium:740063 TEST=emerge-caroline system_api  Change-Id: Ic52205e37cae13d1cc7aaae4b35a634382fb6f66 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/650227 Commit-Ready: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="650227" owner_email="hashimoto@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/system_api" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/system_api" ref="refs/changes/27/650227/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib00cec674e97a4e4a6ad16f26f4bdfa3aea42991" commit="da47abd369727b36ad42a85af3ed663427dbb141" commit_message="virtual_file_provider: Use method call instead of signal  VirtualFileRequestHandlerService is implemented as part of chrome. Call a method of this service instead of sending signals.  BUG=chromium:740063 TEST=emerge-caroline virtual_file_provider CQ-DEPEND=CL:650227  Change-Id: Ib00cec674e97a4e4a6ad16f26f4bdfa3aea42991 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/650228 Commit-Ready: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="650228" owner_email="hashimoto@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/28/650228/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id113dc3add52f4d840854ab180925c48d1a113c5" commit="b1423d43450905715c61e1bc6b8a6b330589ad3c" commit_message="u2fd: add override for device policy  The device policy to enable the U2F feature is hard to set by the user willing to test it (or nearly impossible for unenrolled user). Add a mechanism for easier testing / override for unenrolled users: flag files can be created in /var/lib/u2f/force (e.g 'u2f.force' / 'g2f.force' / 'verbose.force') in order to enable u2f/g2f modes (if unset but not forced disable by the policy) and verbose debugging.  BUG=b:35545754 TEST=manual, using the crosh command in the follow-up CL try the following options: create g2f.force file in /var/lib/u2f/force, then both u2f.force and verbose.force flag files, and verify in /var/log/messages that the daemon is behaving as expected by the flags.  Change-Id: Id113dc3add52f4d840854ab180925c48d1a113c5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/645976 Commit-Ready: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="645976" owner_email="vpalatin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/76/645976/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4289603aa64994864bb00dbef3e832ff3463d317" commit="b8b76a3124c806711718fbc32584af3f5f93b5c0" commit_message="debugd/crosh: add SetU2fFlags command  Add the 'u2f_flags' crosh command to override the lack of device policy setting for the u2fd daemon or get debugging logs. Implement the helper to set the flag files in debugd.  BUG=b:35545754 TEST=manual: in crosh, run 'u2f_flags u2f' and 'u2f_flags g2f,verbose' commands and see u2fd daemon behaving accordingly in /var/log/messages.  Change-Id: I4289603aa64994864bb00dbef3e832ff3463d317 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/650289 Commit-Ready: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="650289" owner_email="vpalatin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/89/650289/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idb524f513dc62f90169307af8bddbb8b27ad0e96" commit="9a7bca3a76a43e4efa8e4f813a8ced63cb3d6b24" commit_message="avtest_label_detect: fix DRM node used for VA-API  Since libva 1.8.3, DRM authentication is now always performed on primary DRM nodes (/dev/dri/card*). This will fail since Chromium clients are expected to use render nodes, and since avtest_label_detect relied on this node this resulted in labels not being assigned properly in lab nodes and video tests not being run.  Fix this by using /dev/dri/renderD* when looking for VA-API features. These nodes to not require authentication and are better suited for that purpose anyway.  BUG=chromium:761949 TEST=Checked that avtest_label_detect was returning the expected labels  Change-Id: Idb524f513dc62f90169307af8bddbb8b27ad0e96 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/654399 Commit-Ready: Alexandre Courbot &lt;acourbot@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alexandre Courbot &lt;acourbot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kuang-che Wu &lt;kcwu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="654399" owner_email="acourbot@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/99/654399/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I31c792d051d5d9b75ef4016e9bb8a080a8a67763" commit="7959ce60fb23ead16b87e353e7